  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> be any two non-zero complex numbers such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> then maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced></math> is<br /><br />Note: In actual paper value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced></math> was asked. Hence, none of the options given were correct. So we have modified the question as well as options."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
